=== Case I: re-derive the constraining quartic ===
4*A in Case I = p^4 - 8*p^3 + 18*p^2 + 8*p + 1
  vs poly_I(p) = p^4 - 8*p^3 + 18*p^2 + 8*p + 1
  difference   = 0

So in Case I the '=5*square' constraint is on A, giving 4A=poly_I(p),
not on B. The earlier '4B' was the trivially-square Pythagorean side.

Cross-check: poly_I(p) = poly_II(-p) ?
  poly_II(-p) = p^4 - 8*p^3 + 18*p^2 + 8*p + 1
  4*A_I       = p^4 - 8*p^3 + 18*p^2 + 8*p + 1
  equal? diff = 0

=> Case I reduces to 20 Z^2 = poly_I(Y) = poly_II(-Y),
   i.e. the SAME curve C_anom under Y -> -Y.  Confirmed.
